          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Like the triangle inequality, can you form a rule that describes the two angles for which a triangle is possible?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.128,
            0.139,
            0.831,
            0.157
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ans",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ": Rules for two angles A and B to form a triangle is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "0^{\\circ} <  A  +  B  < 180^{\\circ}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.192,
            0.252,
            0.209
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Page No. 165",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.133,
            0.221,
            0.299,
            0.239
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Figure it out",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.133,
            0.251,
            0.882,
            0.293
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. Find the third angle of a triangle (using a parallel line) when two of the angles are:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.304,
            0.541,
            0.322
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Process for (a) is given. Try for rest.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.173,
            0.332,
            0.288,
            0.35
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(a) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathbf { 3 6 ^ { \\circ } } , 7 2 ^ { \\circ }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.332,
            0.357,
            0.673,
            0.515
